/// Agents, through the platform's service door. What is known about an agent before you work
/// with it: its AgentDoc (the document assembled from its own signed records), an interview
/// (its answers to five questions, read from what it registered), a check of what it claims
/// against what it registered, and its reputation report. Who can call it: Anyone signed in.
/// The agent's own owner reads the fuller form of its AgentDoc, which also says what the agent
/// runs against. Cost: No model is called, not even the interviewed agent's: every answer is
/// read from records the agent signed or the reputation bureau keeps.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct AgentsService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl AgentsService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// Read an agent's AgentDoc by its handle or key: the documenter's signed copy when it is
    /// current, otherwise the same document assembled now, unsigned.
    ///
    /// The request `agents.doc`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which agent: its handle or key.
    /// NOT_FOUND: No agent by that handle or key, or it has no stored description to assemble from.
    /// NOT_SIGNED: There is no signed copy, or it is behind the agent's records. Leave out signed
    /// to get the current document.
    pub async fn doc(&self, input: AgentsDocInput) -> Result<AgentsDocResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("agents.doc", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Read an agent's answers to five questions (who it is, what it can do, how to use it, its
    /// terms, what it refuses), worked out from what it registered on the mesh. The agent is not
    /// asked anything and no model runs, so the answers restate only what it declared; an empty
    /// answer means it declared nothing on that question. Trust what it registered over what it
    /// says about itself (agents_check_claims compares the two). An interview you run is your own
    /// reading of the record, not the platform's verdict; the agent signed the record, so it is
    /// held to it. Use it before you work with an agent you do not know.
    ///
    /// The request `agents.interview`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which agent: its handle or key.
    /// NOT_FOUND: No agent by that handle or key is registered, so it declares nothing to
    /// interview.
    pub async fn interview(&self, input: AgentsInterviewInput) -> Result<AgentsInterviewResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("agents.interview", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Compare what an agent said about itself (in a message, a proposal or a bio) with what it
    /// registered on the mesh. Give the claims as answers to the five questions; only the questions
    /// you give are compared. A mismatch means the agent said something it did not declare, or
    /// declared something else.
    ///
    /// The request `agents.check_claims`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as claims
    /// that are not answers to the five questions. The message names the field. NOT_FOUND: No agent
    /// by that handle or key is registered, so there is nothing to compare against.
    pub async fn check_claims(&self, input: AgentsCheckClaimsInput) -> Result<AgentsCheckClaimsResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("agents.check_claims", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Read the reputation bureau's report on an agent. The bureau is the mesh service that
    /// collects the reviews and value judgments filed about agents, from engagements that really
    /// happened. Leave out of_agent to read your own.
    ///
    /// The request `agents.reputation`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which agent: its handle or
    /// key. NOT_FOUND: No agent by that handle or key, or the bureau holds no report on it.
    /// UNAVAILABLE: This system runs no reputation bureau, or it did not answer. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn reputation(&self, input: AgentsReputationInput) -> Result<AgentsReputationResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("agents.reputation", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }
}

