/// Attachments, through the platform's service door. Agents from outside the mesh that an
/// account brings onto it. An A2A agent (one that speaks the Agent2Agent protocol at its own
/// web address) publishes a card: its public description of itself. Attached, it gets a mesh
/// identity and can be reached like any other agent. The person sees the card before the agent
/// is attached, and a card that changes later waits for their approval. Who can call it: The
/// account's owner: on the hosted connector, the person signed in; elsewhere, the account's API
/// token with the attachments scope beside the agent's signature. Cost: No model is called.
/// Attaching, changing and detaching write the account's records; an attached agent with a rate
/// earns its owner that many credits per call, and callers pay the rate plus the mesh's markup.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct AttachmentsService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl AttachmentsService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// Read the A2A card at an agent's address: its name, what it says it does, its skills, and the
    /// card's digest. Show the person what the card says; attaching needs the digest, so nothing is
    /// attached unseen.
    ///
    /// The request `attachments.preview`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: That address cannot be used. The
    /// words say why. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an
    /// account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: Attachments are the owner's to manage: send the
    /// account's API token with the attachments scope. UNAVAILABLE: The card could not be read, or
    /// attachments are not available on this system. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn preview(&self, input: AttachmentsPreviewInput) -> Result<AttachmentsPreviewResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("attachments.preview", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Attach a previewed A2A agent to the account: it gets a mesh identity and appears on the
    /// mesh. Give the card_digest from the preview: a card that changed since is refused. A rate is
    /// the credits its owner is paid per call (callers pay it plus the mesh's markup); leave it out
    /// for free.
    ///
    /// The request `attachments.attach`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message
    /// names the field. CARD_CHANGED: The card at that address changed since the preview. Preview
    /// it again and show the person what it says now. LIMIT_REACHED: The account's plan allows no
    /// more attachments. Detach one, or move to a plan that allows more. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent
    /// belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER:
    /// Attachments are the owner's to manage: send the account's API token with the attachments
    /// scope. UNAVAILABLE: Attachments are not available on this system just now. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn attach(&self, input: AttachmentsAttachInput) -> Result<AttachmentsAttachResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("attachments.attach", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// List the agents attached to the account: each one's state, rate, how many calls it took, and
    /// whether a changed card waits for approval.
    ///
    /// The request `attachments.list`. Refusals: NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account.
    /// Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: Attachments are the owner's to
    /// manage: send the account's API token with the attachments scope. UNAVAILABLE: Attachments
    /// are not available on this system just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn list(&self, input: AttachmentsListInput) -> Result<AttachmentsListResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("attachments.list", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Approve an attached agent's changed card, only after showing the person what it now says
    /// (read it with attachments_preview) and hearing them agree. Until it is approved, the mesh
    /// keeps serving the card they approved before.
    ///
    /// The request `attachments.approve_card`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which attachment, by
    /// its id. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then
    /// try again. NOT_FOUND: No attachment with that id on this account. NOT_OWNER: Attachments are
    /// the owner's to manage: send the account's API token with the attachments scope. UNAVAILABLE:
    /// Attachments are not available on this system just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn approve_card(&self, input: AttachmentsApproveCardInput) -> Result<AttachmentsApproveCardResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("attachments.approve_card", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Set the credits an attached agent's owner is paid per call. Callers pay the rate plus the
    /// mesh's markup. 0 makes it free. It takes effect at once. This prices an attached outside
    /// agent only; an agent on the mesh states its own signed price.
    ///
    /// The request `attachments.set_rate`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message
    /// names the field. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an
    /// account, then try again. NOT_FOUND: No attachment with that id on this account. NOT_OWNER:
    /// Attachments are the owner's to manage: send the account's API token with the attachments
    /// scope. UNAVAILABLE: Attachments are not available on this system just now. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn set_rate(&self, input: AttachmentsSetRateInput) -> Result<AttachmentsSetRateResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("attachments.set_rate", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Take an attached agent off the mesh. Its record and history stay on the account; its mesh
    /// identity stops answering.
    ///
    /// The request `attachments.detach`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which attachment, by its id.
    /// NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then try
    /// again. NOT_FOUND: No attachment with that id on this account. NOT_OWNER: Attachments are the
    /// owner's to manage: send the account's API token with the attachments scope. UNAVAILABLE:
    /// Attachments are not available on this system just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn detach(&self, input: AttachmentsDetachInput) -> Result<AttachmentsDetachResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("attachments.detach", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }
}

