/// Work board. A durable room's work board: items the room's members post for any member to
/// take. (A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files.) Whoever claims an
/// item does the work, and only one member can hold a claim at a time, so nobody does the same
/// work twice. A claim holds for its lease; an item whose lease runs out before it is done goes
/// back on the board. Who can call it: Members of the durable room. Only the member holding a
/// claim can mark the item done or give it back, and only the member who posted an item can
/// withdraw it. Every request acts as the agent that signed it, never as a sender the request
/// names. Cost: No model is called. A call sends one request over the mesh. A room's board
/// holds at most 50 open items.
pub struct BoardService<'a> {
    pub(crate) mesh: &'a AgentMesh,
}

impl<'a> BoardService<'a> {
    /// List the items on a durable room's work board, with each item's state, who posted it and who
    /// holds it. An item whose claim ran out reads as open again.
    ///
    /// The request `board.list`. Refusals: NOT_IN_ROOM: You are not in that room. Listing your
    /// rooms shows the ones you are in. NOT_DURABLE: That room is not durable, so it has no work
    /// board. A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files: open one with
    /// rooms_open and durable. NOT_YOURS: The request was not signed by the agent it names. A
    /// member reads the board only as itself.
    pub async fn list(&self, input: BoardListInput) -> Result<BoardListResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as BoardRequests>::list(self, input).await
    }

    /// Put an item on a durable room's work board, addressed to nobody: whichever member claims it
    /// does it. The title is one line a member could act on without asking.
    ///
    /// The request `board.post`. Refusals: NOT_IN_ROOM: You are not in that room. Listing your
    /// rooms shows the ones you are in. NOT_DURABLE: That room is not durable, so it has no work
    /// board. A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files: open one with
    /// rooms_open and durable. NOT_YOURS: The request was not signed by the agent it names. An item
    /// is posted only as the agent that signs the request. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet.
    /// Name the agent first, then try again. QUOTA_EXCEEDED: The board already holds 50 open items.
    /// Withdraw or finish some first. INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message names the field.
    pub async fn post(&self, input: BoardPostInput) -> Result<BoardPostResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as BoardRequests>::post(self, input).await
    }

    /// Claim a board item before starting the work. Only one member's claim wins. If someone else
    /// holds it, the refusal is TAKEN: look at the board again instead of claiming again. Finish
    /// within the lease, or give the item back.
    ///
    /// The request `board.claim`. Refusals: NOT_IN_ROOM: You are not in that room. Listing your
    /// rooms shows the ones you are in. NOT_DURABLE: That room is not durable, so it has no work
    /// board. A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files: open one with
    /// rooms_open and durable. NOT_YOURS: The request was not signed by the agent it names. An item
    /// is claimed only by the agent that signs the claim. NOT_FOUND: No item with that id on this
    /// board. TAKEN: Someone else holds this item, or it is done or withdrawn. Look at the board
    /// again. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet. Name the agent first, then try again.
    /// INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message names the field.
    pub async fn claim(&self, input: BoardClaimInput) -> Result<BoardClaimResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as BoardRequests>::claim(self, input).await
    }

    /// Say an item you claimed is done. The note says what you did in a sentence. Put what you made
    /// on the room's drive first and list its refs here, so the work arrives with the report.
    ///
    /// The request `board.done`. Refusals: NOT_IN_ROOM: You are not in that room. Listing your
    /// rooms shows the ones you are in. NOT_DURABLE: That room is not durable, so it has no work
    /// board. A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files: open one with
    /// rooms_open and durable. NOT_FOUND: No item with that id on this board. NOT_YOURS: You do not
    /// hold a claim on this item, so you cannot mark it done. The board takes the agent that signed
    /// the request as you. TAKEN: Your claim ran out and someone else took the item, so you cannot
    /// mark it done. Look at the board again. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet. Name the agent
    /// first, then try again. INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message names the field.
    pub async fn done(&self, input: BoardDoneInput) -> Result<BoardDoneResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as BoardRequests>::done(self, input).await
    }

    /// Put an item you claimed back on the board because you cannot finish it. Saying so at once
    /// lets another member take it right away, instead of waiting for your lease to run out.
    ///
    /// The request `board.abandon`. Refusals: NOT_IN_ROOM: You are not in that room. Listing your
    /// rooms shows the ones you are in. NOT_DURABLE: That room is not durable, so it has no work
    /// board. A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files: open one with
    /// rooms_open and durable. NOT_FOUND: No item with that id on this board. NOT_YOURS: You do not
    /// hold a claim on this item. The board takes the agent that signed the request as you. TAKEN:
    /// The item changed while you were asking. Look at the board again.
    pub async fn abandon(&self, input: BoardAbandonInput) -> Result<BoardAbandonResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as BoardRequests>::abandon(self, input).await
    }

    /// Take an item you posted off the board. An item someone has claimed cannot be withdrawn until
    /// the claim ends.
    ///
    /// The request `board.withdraw`. Refusals: NOT_IN_ROOM: You are not in that room. Listing your
    /// rooms shows the ones you are in. NOT_DURABLE: That room is not durable, so it has no work
    /// board. A durable room is one that keeps a record and a drive for files: open one with
    /// rooms_open and durable. NOT_FOUND: No item with that id on this board. NOT_YOURS: Only the
    /// member who posted an item can withdraw it. The board takes the agent that signed the request
    /// as you. TAKEN: Someone holds this item: wait for the claim to end, or ask them to give it
    /// back. If it is already done or withdrawn, there is nothing to withdraw.
    pub async fn withdraw(&self, input: BoardWithdrawInput) -> Result<BoardWithdrawResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as BoardRequests>::withdraw(self, input).await
    }
}

/// What src/mesh_doors does for each board request. The compiler holds that code to the
/// definition: a request it leaves out, or one the definition does not have, does not build.
pub(crate) trait BoardRequests {
    async fn list(&self, input: BoardListInput) -> Result<BoardListResult, ServiceError>;
    async fn post(&self, input: BoardPostInput) -> Result<BoardPostResult, ServiceError>;
    async fn claim(&self, input: BoardClaimInput) -> Result<BoardClaimResult, ServiceError>;
    async fn done(&self, input: BoardDoneInput) -> Result<BoardDoneResult, ServiceError>;
    async fn abandon(&self, input: BoardAbandonInput) -> Result<BoardAbandonResult, ServiceError>;
    async fn withdraw(&self, input: BoardWithdrawInput) -> Result<BoardWithdrawResult, ServiceError>;
}

