/// Credits, through the platform's service door. An account's credits, the mesh's unit of
/// account: the balance, how much was granted, earned and spent, the ways the account pays in,
/// the latest statement lines, the spending allowance registered for each of its agents, and
/// the budget its agents may commit to without a person. Owning an agent with a price earns
/// credits at the rate set for it. Who can call it: The account's owner: on the hosted
/// connector, the person signed in; elsewhere, the account's API token with the credits scope
/// beside the agent's signature. Cost: Free, and no model is called. A request reads or writes
/// the account's records; idle, the service costs nothing.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct CreditsService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl CreditsService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// Read the account's credits: the balance, what was granted, earned and spent, how the account
    /// pays in, and the latest ten statement lines.
    ///
    /// The request `credits.summary`. Refusals: NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account.
    /// Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: Credits are the owner's to read:
    /// send the account's API token with the credits scope. UNAVAILABLE: Credits are not enabled on
    /// this system, or the ledger could not be read just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn summary(&self, input: CreditsSummaryInput) -> Result<CreditsSummaryResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("credits.summary", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// The spending allowance registered with the platform for one of your agents, and what that
    /// agent reports spending against it: per currency, per day and per context, with any ceiling
    /// it went over. Send a signed allowance document to register it, replacing the one held. The
    /// allowance itself is enforced on the machine that runs the agent; registering it lets the
    /// owner's view mark spend that went over.
    ///
    /// The request `credits.allowance`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, or the document
    /// is not a validly signed allowance for that agent. The words say which. NO_ACCOUNT: This
    /// agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: An
    /// agent's allowance is the owner's to read and register: send the account's API token with the
    /// credits scope. NOT_YOURS: That is not one of your agents. NOT_YOUR_KEY: The document's
    /// owner_key is not a key your account holds. A document signed by somebody else's key is
    /// somebody else's policy. UNAVAILABLE: Allowances or spend reports are not kept on this
    /// system, or could not be read just now.
    pub async fn allowance(&self, input: CreditsAllowanceInput) -> Result<CreditsAllowanceResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("credits.allowance", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// The account's standing budget for what its agents may agree to without a person: the most
    /// one task may cost before a person must say yes, and whether every agreement waits for a
    /// person. Send max_per_task or require_person to tighten it. Raising it, or letting agents
    /// agree alone, takes the owner's passkey in the app.
    ///
    /// The request `credits.budget`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The words say
    /// which. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then
    /// try again. NOT_OWNER: The budget is the owner's: send the account's API token with the
    /// credits scope. NEEDS_PASSKEY: That would raise the budget or let agents agree alone, which
    /// takes the owner's passkey in the app. loosen_at says where. UNAVAILABLE: The account could
    /// not be read or written just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn budget(&self, input: CreditsBudgetInput) -> Result<CreditsBudgetResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("credits.budget", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }
}

