/// Debt, through the platform's service door. The ledger keeps one record, with one numbering,
/// for two kinds of debt. Dependency debt is owed to the owner of something that depends on a
/// change. It has a deadline, and until it is closed it holds back the acts it names (update,
/// promote, rollback or decommission) on the changed agent or solution. Technical debt is what
/// the AgentMesh team owes itself, and it holds nothing back. The four requests here are the
/// ones the ledger defines (services/src/ledger/requests.ts). Who can call it: The owner of an
/// agent or a solution reads the items against it. The platform files items and moves them,
/// with the ledger's key (the debt scope); operators with the read or reports scope read every
/// item. Cost: No model is called. A call is a read or a write of the ledger's database.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct DebtService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl DebtService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// File one item; the ledger gives it the next number.
    ///
    /// The request `debt.file`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is missing or out of shape. The
    /// words say which. NUMBER_TAKEN: The number named was not reserved for this caller, or another
    /// item has it. NOT_OPERATOR: Only the platform files debt, with the ledger's key (the debt
    /// scope). UNAVAILABLE: The ledger has no database on this system, or did not answer.
    pub async fn file(&self, input: DebtFileInput) -> Result<DebtFileResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("debt.file", crate::services::KeyUse::Operator, &input).await
    }

    /// Items by kind, state, asset, whom they are owed to, or the act they hold back, newest number
    /// first. An owner names their own agents or solutions in against and sees the items against
    /// them; an operator may list everything.
    ///
    /// The request `debt.list`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A filter takes a word it does not know, or
    /// an owner named no asset. The words say which. NOT_YOURS: You named an agent or a solution
    /// that is not yours. Owners see only the items against their own. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent
    /// belongs to no account, so it owns nothing to ask about. UNAVAILABLE: The ledger has no
    /// database on this system, or did not answer.
    pub async fn list(&self, input: DebtListInput) -> Result<DebtListResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("debt.list", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// One item, with every change of its state: who, when, the door and the evidence.
    ///
    /// The request `debt.show`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which item: its number. NOT_FOUND: No
    /// item with that number that you may see. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account, so it
    /// owns nothing to ask about. UNAVAILABLE: The ledger has no database on this system, or did
    /// not answer.
    pub async fn show(&self, input: DebtShowInput) -> Result<DebtShowResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("debt.show", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Move one item to a new state, saying who and with what evidence. An item that is resolved,
    /// overridden or dropped can only be opened again. Resolving, dropping, overriding and opening
    /// again each need evidence. Only dependency debt can be overridden, and only once its deadline
    /// has passed.
    ///
    /// The request `debt.transition`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is missing or out of shape.
    /// The words say which. NOT_FOUND: No item with that number. NOT_ALLOWED: That move is not
    /// allowed. The words say why. NOT_OPERATOR: Only the platform moves debt, with the ledger's
    /// key (the debt scope). UNAVAILABLE: The ledger has no database on this system, or did not
    /// answer.
    pub async fn transition(&self, input: DebtTransitionInput) -> Result<DebtTransitionResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("debt.transition", crate::services::KeyUse::Operator, &input).await
    }
}

