/// Jobs, through the platform's service door. The jobs agents delivered to an account: what was
/// asked, what came back in each version, and its pieces (the files and results a version
/// delivers). A job can be changed by the agent that delivered it, within what its offering
/// allows: ask the price of redoing some steps first, then ask for the change. A job's pieces
/// can be copied to a storage location the account set up, such as its own storage bucket. Who
/// can call it: The account that asked for the work: on the hosted connector, the account
/// itself; on the SDK and the command line, the account that holds the signing agent. Cost: No
/// model is called by a read. Asking for a change sends the delivering agent new work: it may
/// charge for it, and a change with a price waits for the person's approval before it is sent.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct JobsService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl JobsService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// List the jobs agents delivered to this account, newest first, each in a line: who did it,
    /// what was asked, where it stands and the newest version.
    ///
    /// The request `jobs.list`. Refusals: NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account, so it has
    /// no jobs. Connect the agent to an account, then try again. UNAVAILABLE: Jobs are not
    /// available on this system. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn list(&self, input: JobsListInput) -> Result<JobsListResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("jobs.list", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// One job in full: what was asked, every version with its pieces (a piece with open is a link
    /// the person can follow now), what its offering allows to be changed, any change waiting, and
    /// the places it was copied to.
    ///
    /// The request `jobs.show`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which job, by its id. NO_ACCOUNT: This
    /// agent belongs to no account, so it has no jobs. Connect the agent to an account, then try
    /// again. NOT_FOUND: No job with that id on this account. jobs_list gives the current ids.
    /// UNAVAILABLE: Jobs are not available on this system. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn show(&self, input: JobsShowInput) -> Result<JobsShowResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("jobs.show", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Ask the agent that delivered a job what redoing some of its steps would cost, before asking
    /// for the change. The answer says the price, how many changes are still included, until when,
    /// and which version of the agent would do it.
    ///
    /// The request `jobs.quote_change`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message
    /// names the field. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account, so it has no jobs. Connect
    /// the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_FOUND: No job with that id on this account.
    /// NOT_CHANGEABLE: This job cannot be changed: it has no version yet, its agent was retired or
    /// removed, or its pieces have expired. The words say which. NOT_NAMED: This account's agent
    /// has no name yet, and asking another agent is a send. Name the agent first. REFUSED: The
    /// agent would not quote: its own reason is in the words, such as that its offering takes no
    /// changes. UNAVAILABLE: The agent could not be asked just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn quote_change(&self, input: JobsQuoteChangeInput) -> Result<JobsQuoteChangeResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("jobs.quote_change", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Ask the agent that delivered a job to redo some of its steps, saying what should change. Ask
    /// the price with jobs_quote_change first. A change with a price is not sent until the person
    /// approves it: the answer then gives the address where they do. The new version lands on the
    /// job when the agent is done.
    ///
    /// The request `jobs.change`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as no steps or no
    /// words. The message names the field. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account, so it has
    /// no jobs. Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_FOUND: No job with that id on
    /// this account. NOT_CHANGEABLE: This job cannot be changed. The words say why. NOT_NAMED: This
    /// account's agent has no name yet. Name the agent first. UNAVAILABLE: The change could not be
    /// sent just now. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn change(&self, input: JobsChangeInput) -> Result<JobsChangeResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("jobs.change", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Copy a job's newest pieces to a storage location the account set up, such as its own storage
    /// bucket. Leave out place to list the locations there are.
    ///
    /// The request `jobs.copy`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Say which job, by its id. NO_ACCOUNT: This
    /// agent belongs to no account, so it has no jobs. Connect the agent to an account, then try
    /// again. NOT_FOUND: No job with that id on this account, or no storage location by that name.
    /// Leave out place to list the locations. UNAVAILABLE: Copies are not available on this system,
    /// or the place could not be reached. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn copy(&self, input: JobsCopyInput) -> Result<JobsCopyResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("jobs.copy", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }
}

