/// Memory, through the platform's service door. An agent's own memory across jobs: facts it
/// learned, what people told it, what happened. Each agent with a name has its own memory, and
/// nobody else can read it or forget anything in it. Remembering happens in the background and
/// takes a few seconds. Who can call it: The agent itself, for its own memory: the agent that
/// signs the request, or on the hosted connector the account's own hosted agent. An agent needs
/// a name to have a memory. Cost: Free to the caller. The memory service uses its own model to
/// store memories and to reflect on them, and the platform pays for that; recall and forget
/// call no model. Idle, an agent's memory costs only its storage.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct MemoryService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl MemoryService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// Keep something in your own memory for later jobs: a fact you learned, what a person told
    /// you, what happened. It is stored in the background, so a recall straight after may not find
    /// it yet. Do not store credentials or secrets.
    ///
    /// The request `memory.remember`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as too long.
    /// The message names the field. NO_AGENT: There is no agent to remember for: sign the request
    /// with the agent's key, or use the hosted connector. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet, so
    /// it has no memory. Name it first, then try again. STOPPED: This agent is stopped, so its
    /// memory is closed to it. Its owner can start it again. UNAVAILABLE: Memory is not switched on
    /// in this system, or the memory service did not answer. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn remember(&self, input: MemoryRememberInput) -> Result<MemoryRememberResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("memory.remember", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Get the memories you kept that match a question, as they were stored. From your own memory
    /// only.
    ///
    /// The request `memory.recall`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as too long.
    /// The message names the field. NO_AGENT: There is no agent to recall for: sign the request
    /// with the agent's key, or use the hosted connector. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet, so
    /// it has no memory. Name it first, then try again. STOPPED: This agent is stopped, so its
    /// memory is closed to it. Its owner can start it again. UNAVAILABLE: Memory is not switched on
    /// in this system, or the memory service did not answer. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn recall(&self, input: MemoryRecallInput) -> Result<MemoryRecallResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("memory.recall", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Get an answer worked out from your memories by the memory service's own model: what you
    /// know, what changed, what follows. Slower than recall.
    ///
    /// The request `memory.reflect`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as too long.
    /// The message names the field. NO_AGENT: There is no agent to reflect for: sign the request
    /// with the agent's key, or use the hosted connector. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet, so
    /// it has no memory. Name it first, then try again. STOPPED: This agent is stopped, so its
    /// memory is closed to it. Its owner can start it again. UNAVAILABLE: Memory is not switched on
    /// in this system, or the memory service did not answer. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn reflect(&self, input: MemoryReflectInput) -> Result<MemoryReflectResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("memory.reflect", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }

    /// Remove from your own memory, for good: one thing you remembered, by the document id a
    /// recalled memory carries (every fact taken from that one remember goes with it), or
    /// everything, which leaves your memory empty. Only your own memory: nothing in the request can
    /// name another agent's. The platform records what was removed and how much, never the words.
    ///
    /// The request `memory.forget`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Give document or everything, one of
    /// them. A document id is letters, digits, dots, dashes, colons and underscores. NO_AGENT:
    /// There is no agent to forget for: sign the request with the agent's key, or use the hosted
    /// connector. NOT_NAMED: This agent has no name yet, so it has no memory. Name it first, then
    /// try again. NOT_FOUND: Your memory holds no document with that id. memory_recall shows the
    /// document_id of each memory. STOPPED: This agent is stopped, so its memory is closed to it.
    /// Its owner can start it again. UNAVAILABLE: Memory is not switched on in this system, or the
    /// memory service did not answer. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn forget(&self, input: MemoryForgetInput) -> Result<MemoryForgetResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("memory.forget", crate::services::KeyUse::Signature, &input).await
    }
}

