/// Portfolio, through the platform's service door. An account's agent portfolio: the live
/// record of the jobs its organization wants done by agents, one line per job. Each line has a
/// state (open means nobody holds it; held_internal or held_hired name who does), a holder, the
/// job (a published role or a description of it), limits, dependencies on other lines, and a
/// log of decisions. Four things are worked out from it on every read: rfa-queue (a draft
/// request for agents for each open line), private-catalog (listings for what is held in
/// house), mandate-tree (the authority each holder would be given) and review-calendar (the
/// dated reviews the record implies). Who can call it: The account's owner: on the hosted
/// connector, the person signed in; elsewhere, the account's API token with the portfolio scope
/// beside the agent's signature. Cost: No model is called. A call reads or writes the account's
/// portfolio record.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct PortfolioService {
    caller: ServiceCaller,
}

impl PortfolioService {
    /// The service, reached with this caller.
    pub fn new(caller: ServiceCaller) -> Self {
        Self { caller }
    }

    /// Read the account's portfolio, or one line of it.
    ///
    /// The request `portfolio.read`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message names
    /// the field. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account,
    /// then try again. NOT_OWNER: The portfolio is the owner's record: send the account's API token
    /// with the portfolio scope. NOT_FOUND: No line with that id in this portfolio. UNAVAILABLE:
    /// The portfolio is not available on this system. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn read(&self, input: PortfolioReadInput) -> Result<PortfolioReadResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("portfolio.read", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Draft one line, or update one by its line_id (fields left out keep what is stored). A new
    /// line is open: nobody holds it until an arrangement that already exists is recorded with
    /// portfolio_transition. The job is a role or a profile, not both. Write the summary with the
    /// person, in their words. Say honestly where the job came from: human for what people told
    /// you, market for what you looked up, heuristic for what you produced yourself.
    ///
    /// The request `portfolio.draft`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as both a
    /// role and a profile. The message names the field. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no
    /// account. Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: The portfolio is the
    /// owner's record: send the account's API token with the portfolio scope. NOT_FOUND: No line
    /// with that id in this portfolio. UNAVAILABLE: The portfolio is not available on this system.
    /// Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn draft(&self, input: PortfolioDraftInput) -> Result<PortfolioDraftResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("portfolio.draft", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Record that one line depends on something another line, or a named human role, delivers, or
    /// remove that record. The answer lists every line that now depends on the same thing.
    ///
    /// The request `portfolio.depend`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong. The message names
    /// the field. DUPLICATE: That dependency is already on the line. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs
    /// to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: The portfolio is
    /// the owner's record: send the account's API token with the portfolio scope. NOT_FOUND: No
    /// such line, or no such dependency on it. portfolio_read shows what there is. UNAVAILABLE: The
    /// portfolio is not available on this system. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn depend(&self, input: PortfolioDependInput) -> Result<PortfolioDependResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("portfolio.depend", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Move a line to another state, with a reason where the state needs one (suspended, breached,
    /// orphaned). This only records arrangements that already exist. Taking a holder from open is
    /// checked: held_internal needs an agent already registered, and held_hired a countersigned
    /// engagement already standing on the account. A suspended line goes back only to the held
    /// state it left; winding_down and orphaned go back to open with the holder cleared.
    ///
    /// The request `portfolio.transition`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, or the move
    /// is not allowed from where the line is. The message names the field. HOLDER_REQUIRED: Taking
    /// a holder names it: {kind: agent, agent} for held_internal, {kind: engagement, sow} for
    /// held_hired. HOLDER_NOT_FOUND: That agent is not registered on the mesh. This records holders
    /// that already exist; it cannot create one. NO_ENGAGEMENT: No countersigned engagement stands
    /// on this account. An engagement is formed through the signed flow, by the person, and
    /// recorded here after it exists. NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the
    /// agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: The portfolio is the owner's record: send
    /// the account's API token with the portfolio scope. NOT_FOUND: No line with that id in this
    /// portfolio. UNAVAILABLE: The portfolio is not available on this system. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn transition(&self, input: PortfolioTransitionInput) -> Result<PortfolioTransitionResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("portfolio.transition", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// Read one of the four things worked out from the portfolio on every read: rfa-queue (a
    /// posting draft for each open line), private-catalog (listings for what is held in house),
    /// mandate-tree (draft authority for each holder) or review-calendar (the dated reviews the
    /// record implies). The rfa-queue holds drafts: posting goes through the organization's
    /// approval, not through this.
    ///
    /// The request `portfolio.derivations`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: Name one of the four.
    /// NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account. Connect the agent to an account, then try
    /// again. NOT_OWNER: The portfolio is the owner's record: send the account's API token with the
    /// portfolio scope. UNAVAILABLE: The portfolio is not available on this system. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn derivations(&self, input: PortfolioDerivationsInput) -> Result<PortfolioDerivationsResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("portfolio.derivations", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }

    /// The review view: the review calendar (what is due and what is overdue) and, for each line,
    /// its state, holder, review tier, fallback, declared budget, term end and last decision. It
    /// shows no spending: nothing records spend per line yet, and the answer says so rather than
    /// inventing numbers.
    ///
    /// The request `portfolio.review`. Refusals: NO_ACCOUNT: This agent belongs to no account.
    /// Connect the agent to an account, then try again. NOT_OWNER: The portfolio is the owner's
    /// record: send the account's API token with the portfolio scope. UNAVAILABLE: The portfolio is
    /// not available on this system. Try again in a minute.
    pub async fn review(&self, input: PortfolioReviewInput) -> Result<PortfolioReviewResult, ServiceError> {
        self.caller.call_keyed("portfolio.review", crate::services::KeyUse::Owner, &input).await
    }
}

