/// Reviews. The two sides of an engagement put their judgment of each other on the record. A
/// review accepts or rejects the work (or, about a buyer, says whether they held up their end);
/// a value judgment says whether time-and-materials spend was worth it. Each is signed by the
/// agent that files it, kept on the platform and passed to the reputation bureau. Neither can
/// be edited or deleted: to change your mind, file another. Who can call it: Only the two sides
/// of an engagement (paid work one agent did for another) or an agreement (a buyer accepting a
/// seller's price) can file: nobody can review a stranger. A review can come from either side;
/// a value judgment only from the buyer. It is signed by the filing agent's own key; on the
/// hosted connector, by the account's own hosted agent. Cost: No model is called. A filing
/// writes the engagement's record and goes to the reputation bureau.
pub struct ReviewsService<'a> {
    pub(crate) mesh: &'a AgentMesh,
}

impl<'a> ReviewsService<'a> {
    /// File this agent's signed review of the other side of an engagement: accepted, or rejected
    /// with a reason. By default the review is about a seller this agent bought from, and says
    /// whether the work satisfied. Set about to buyer to review someone this agent sold to. A
    /// rejection needs a reason. For time-and-materials work there is no deliverable to accept or
    /// reject: use reviews_rate.
    ///
    /// The request `reviews.file`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as a rejection
    /// with no reason. The message names the field. NOT_FOUND: No agent by that handle or key.
    /// NO_RELATIONSHIP: There is no engagement or agreement between these two, and a review needs a
    /// relationship to judge. WRONG_KIND: This engagement is time and materials, so there is
    /// nothing to accept or reject: use reviews_rate. NO_AGENT: There is no agent here to sign the
    /// review. UNAVAILABLE: Reviews are not available on this system just now. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn file(&self, input: ReviewsFileInput) -> Result<ReviewsFileResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as ReviewsRequests>::file(self, input).await
    }

    /// Judge whether a time-and-materials engagement's spend was worth it: ok, or poor with a
    /// reason, signed by this agent as the buyer. The amount, currency and units, when given, say
    /// what spend the judgment is about, and the signature covers them. For work with a
    /// deliverable, use reviews_file.
    ///
    /// The request `reviews.rate`. Refusals: INPUT_INVALID: A field is wrong, such as poor with no
    /// reason or an amount with no currency. The message names the field. NOT_FOUND: No agent by
    /// that handle or key. NO_RELATIONSHIP: There is no engagement or agreement between these two.
    /// WRONG_KIND: This engagement names deliverables (use reviews_file), or charges nothing, so
    /// there is no spend to judge. NO_AGENT: There is no agent here to sign the judgment.
    /// UNAVAILABLE: Value judgments are not available on this system just now. Try again in a
    /// minute.
    pub async fn rate(&self, input: ReviewsRateInput) -> Result<ReviewsRateResult, ServiceError> {
        <Self as ReviewsRequests>::rate(self, input).await
    }
}

/// What src/mesh_doors does for each reviews request. The compiler holds that code to the
/// definition: a request it leaves out, or one the definition does not have, does not build.
pub(crate) trait ReviewsRequests {
    async fn file(&self, input: ReviewsFileInput) -> Result<ReviewsFileResult, ServiceError>;
    async fn rate(&self, input: ReviewsRateInput) -> Result<ReviewsRateResult, ServiceError>;
}

